From 9ce661e6cbfdf4b85ed1c5791caed58419d0ab6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:01:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(api-mode): optional LeenTrack PHP API backend behind
 NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL (inventory slice)

Build-time switch (lib/api/mode.ts): with NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL unset the app is exactly the existing Supabase app
(legacy providers only renamed and wrapped). With it set, the app talks to the PHP API instead.

- lib/api: dependency-free client (envelope, single-flight refresh, single-flight resume, X-Business-Id, offline != signed out)
- contexts/api-session.tsx: API-backed useAuth()/useBusiness() with the same shapes and the same error wording the pages look for
- lib/data/products.ts: Inventory data access with legacy (unchanged Supabase queries) and API implementations
- app/inventory and the low-stock banner use the data layer; unmigrated screens show a notice in API mode instead of calling Supabase
- tsconfig: allowImportingTsExtensions (lets the client be unit-tested with plain node)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
